-> Enum stands for Enumeration.
-> It is used to define a fixed set of related values.
Basic enum:
----------
enum TrafficSignal {
    case red
    case yellow
    case green
}
var signal = TrafficSignal.red
print(signal)-----> red

Enum with switch:
-----------------
enum TrafficSignal {
    case red, yellow, green
}
var signal = TrafficSignal.green
switch signal {
case .red:
    print("Stop")
case .yellow:
    print("Get Ready")
case .green:
    print("Go")------->OUTPUT  "Go"
}

Enum with raw values:
---------------------
-> Enums can also have predefined values.

enum Day: Int {
    case monday = 1
    case tuesday = 2
    case wednesday = 3
}
print(Day.monday.rawValue)---->1
print(Day.tuesday.rawValue)---->2
